\section*{Analytic path selection at several exponential ends}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Degenerating Ricci-flat tree inequality}: The companion claims that the renormalized Einstein--Hilbert error is little-oh of a scale-neutral weighted Ricci error along the specified finite trees with diverging joining lengths. It also proves the asymptotic path-selection theorem used in that comparison.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Degenerating Ricci-flat tree inequality}: Power-logarithmic expansions in exponential neck variables are kept with recursively compatible remainder estimates, rather than assumed to be convergent analytic series. A path-selection argument realizes finite sign conditions and prescribed limits along analytic paths in ordinary parameters. Applying this to the finite tree’s asymptotic geometry converts a failing elliptic estimate into an impossible selected path.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Degenerating Ricci-flat tree inequality}: The companion claims that the renormalized Einstein--Hilbert error is little-oh of a scale-neutral weighted Ricci error along the specified finite trees with diverging joining lengths. It also proves the asymptotic path-selection theorem used in that comparison. The parameters, regularity assumptions and normalization in this question are retained in applying that assertion.

With the hypotheses and conventions above, the claimed result addresses the whole mathematical assertion on this page.

\subsection{Formal verification}
\textit{Degenerating Ricci-flat tree inequality}: The pinned catalogue lists no Lean formalization for this result.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

